{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_fkFcWn9JTl7G8jn58cmESLDo","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→<!-- Generated on 2026-02-18 -->\n     2→<!-- SE3 Version: 2.5.0 -->\n     3→<!-- Checksum: 42882fbead24daeb410910cc3d0af8bd69ec880c54f694ebb2296ee5cd7b6c34 -->\n     4→\n     5→<!--\n     6→  SE 3.0 Framework Reference File\n     7→  ===============================\n     8→  This file is installed by `se3 init` and serves as the official framework specification.\n     9→\n    10→  Generated File: DO NOT MODIFY DIRECTLY\n    11→  Version: {{SE3_VERSION}}\n    12→  Checksum: {{CHECKSUM}}\n    13→-->\n    14→\n    15→# {{PROJECT_NAME}}\n    16→\n    17→> **Note**: SE3 2.x+ 采用\"手动触发\"模式。不再指望 agent 自觉遵循，而是通过 command 调用。\n    18→\n    19→## SE3 Command 入口\n    20→\n    21→| Command | 用途 |\n    22→|---------|------|\n    23→| `/se3:start` | 开始会话 |\n    24→| `/se3:work <描述>` | 开始/继续工作 |\n    25→| `/se3:done` | 结束会话 |\n    26→\n    27→所有工作流通过 CLI (`se3 start`, `se3 work`, `se3 done`) 程序化驱动，返回 JSON actions 数组。\n    28→\n    29→## Git Commit\n    30→\n    31→使用 `se3 commit` 代替 `git commit`。\n    32→\n    33→```bash\n    34→se3 commit -m \"描述\" -f \"file1.py file2.py\"\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→## Session Guard (2.1+)\n    38→\n    39→- `se3 work` 和 `se3 done` 会检查 session 是否已通过 `se3 start` 启动\n    40→- 未启动时返回错误，提示先运行 `se3 start`\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e569dacb-b70b-4c90-930f-0ca840cf5264","uuid":"a103dfb0-b091-40d4-8e59-a847a914b0cd","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/verify-openspec-commands/.claude/SE3.md","content":"<!-- Generated on 2026-02-18 -->\n<!-- SE3 Version: 2.5.0 -->\n<!-- Checksum: 42882fbead24daeb410910cc3d0af8bd69ec880c54f694ebb2296ee5cd7b6c34 -->\n\n<!--\n  SE 3.0 Framework Reference File\n  ===============================\n  This file is installed by `se3 init` and serves as the official framework specification.\n\n  Generated File: DO NOT MODIFY DIRECTLY\n  Version: {{SE3_VERSION}}\n  Checksum: {{CHECKSUM}}\n-->\n\n# {{PROJECT_NAME}}\n\n> **Note**: SE3 2.x+ 采用\"手动触发\"模式。不再指望 agent 自觉遵循，而是通过 command 调用。\n\n## SE3 Command 入口\n\n| Command | 用途 |\n|---------|------|\n| `/se3:start` | 开始会话 |\n| `/se3:work <描述>` | 开始/继续工作 |\n| `/se3:done` | 结束会话 |\n\n所有工作流通过 CLI (`se3 start`, `se3 work`, `se3 done`) 程序化驱动，返回 JSON actions 数组。\n\n## Git Commit\n\n使用 `se3 commit` 代替 `git commit`。\n\n```bash\nse3 commit -m \"描述\" -f \"file1.py file2.py\"\n```\n\n## Session Guard (2.1+)\n\n- `se3 work` 和 `se3 done` 会检查 session 是否已通过 `se3 start` 启动\n- 未启动时返回错误，提示先运行 `se3 start`","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_GrGhf7FZCetjYV15NbGWEsiq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"OpenSpec CLI commands for SE 3.0.\n     2→\n     3→Provides commands for managing the openspec/ directory structure:\n     4→- openspec init: Initialize the openspec/ directory structure\n     5→- openspec list --specs: List all available specs\n     6→\"\"\"\n     7→\n     8→import json\n     9→from pathlib import Path\n    10→from typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\n    11→\n    12→import typer\n    13→\n    14→from ..utils import parse_spec\n    15→\n    16→app = typer.Typer(name=\"openspec\", help=\"Manage OpenSpec directory and specs\")\n    17→\n    18→\n    19→def initialize_openspec(project_root: Path, force: bool = False) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    20→    \"\"\"\n    21→    Initialize the openspec/ directory structure.\n    22→\n    23→    Args:\n    24→        project_root: Root directory of the project\n    25→        force: Reinitialize even if already exists\n    26→\n    27→    Returns:\n    28→        Dict with created directories and status\n    29→    \"\"\"\n    30→    result = {\n    31→        \"created\": [],\n    32→        \"existing\": [],\n    33→        \"success\": True,\n    34→        \"message\": \"\",\n    35→    }\n    36→\n    37→    openspec_dir = project_root / \"openspec\"\n    38→\n    39→    # Check if already initialized\n    40→    if openspec_dir.exists() and not force:\n    41→        # Check if all required subdirectories exist\n    42→        required_dirs = [\"specs\", \"changes\", \"changes/archive\"]\n    43→        all_exist = all((openspec_dir / d).exists() for d in required_dirs)\n    44→\n    45→        if all_exist:\n    46→            result[\"message\"] = \"OpenSpec directory already initialized. Use --force to reinitialize.\"\n    47→            result[\"existing\"] = [str(openspec_dir / d) for d in required_dirs]\n    48→            return result\n    49→\n    50→    # Create directory structure\n    51→    dirs_to_create = [\n    52→        openspec_dir / \"specs\",\n    53→        openspec_dir / \"changes\",\n    54→        openspec_dir / \"changes\" / \"archive\",\n    55→    ]\n    56→\n    57→    for dir_path in dirs_to_create:\n    58→        if dir_path.exists():\n    59→            result[\"existing\"].append(str(dir_path))\n    60→        else:\n    61→            dir_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    62→            result[\"created\"].append(str(dir_path))\n    63→\n    64→    result[\"message\"] = f\"OpenSpec initialized: {len(result['created'])} directories created\"\n    65→    return result\n    66→\n    67→\n    68→def list_specs(project_root: Path) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    69→    \"\"\"\n    70→    List all available specs in openspec/specs/.\n    71→\n    72→    Args:\n    73→        project_root: Root directory of the project\n    74→\n    75→    Returns:\n    76→        List of spec dicts with name, path, and purpose\n    77→    \"\"\"\n    78→    specs = []\n    79→    specs_dir = project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n    80→\n    81→    if not specs_dir.exists():\n    82→        return specs\n    83→\n    84→    for spec_dir in sorted(specs_dir.iterdir()):\n    85→        if not spec_dir.is_dir():\n    86→            continue\n    87→\n    88→        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n    89→        if not spec_file.exists():\n    90→            continue\n    91→\n    92→        spec_info = {\n    93→            \"name\": spec_dir.name,\n    94→            \"path\": str(spec_file.relative_to(project_root)),\n    95→            \"purpose\": None,\n    96→        }\n    97→\n    98→        # Try to parse the spec file to extract purpose\n    99→        try:\n   100→            parsed = parse_spec(str(spec_file))\n   101→            if parsed.get(\"purpose\"):\n   102→                spec_info[\"purpose\"] = parsed[\"purpose\"]\n   103→        except Exception:\n   104→            pass\n   105→\n   106→        specs.append(spec_info)\n   107→\n   108→    return specs\n   109→\n   110→\n   111→@app.callback()\n   112→def openspec_callback(ctx: typer.Context):\n   113→    \"\"\"Manage OpenSpec directory and specs.\"\"\"\n   114→    pass\n   115→\n   116→\n   117→@app.command(name=\"init\")\n   118→def init_cmd(\n   119→    force: bool = typer.Option(\n   120→        False,\n   121→        \"--force\",\n   122→        \"-f\",\n   123→        help=\"Reinitialize even if already initialized\",\n   124→    ),\n   125→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\n   126→        \".\",\n   127→        \"--project-root\",\n   128→        \"-p\",\n   129→        help=\"Root directory of the project\",\n   130→    ),\n   131→    format: str = typer.Option(\n   132→        \"text\",\n   133→        \"--format\",\n   134→        \"-f\",\n   135→        help=\"Output format (text or json)\",\n   136→    ),\n   137→):\n   138→    \"\"\"Initialize the openspec/ directory structure.\n   139→\n   140→    Creates the following directories:\n   141→    - openspec/specs/        # Source of truth for requirements\n   142→    - openspec/changes/      # Active changes\n   143→    - openspec/changes/archive/  # Archived changes\n   144→    \"\"\"\n   145→    root = Path(project_root).resolve()\n   146→    result = initialize_openspec(root, force)\n   147→\n   148→    if format == \"json\":\n   149→        typer.echo(json.dumps(result, indent=2, default=str))\n   150→    else:\n   151→        if result[\"created\"]:\n   152→            typer.echo(typer.style(\"Created directories:\", fg=typer.colors.GREEN))\n   153→            for d in result[\"created\"]:\n   154→                typer.echo(f\"  - {d}\")\n   155→\n   156→        if result[\"existing\"]:\n   157→            typer.echo(typer.style(\"Existing directories:\", fg=typer.colors.YELLOW))\n   158→            for d in result[\"existing\"]:\n   159→                typer.echo(f\"  - {d}\")\n   160→\n   161→        typer.echo(f\"\\n{result['message']}\")\n   162→\n   163→    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if result[\"success\"] else 1)\n   164→\n   165→\n   166→@app.command(name=\"list\")\n   167→def list_cmd(\n   168→    specs: bool = typer.Option(\n   169→        False,\n   170→        \"--specs\",\n   171→        \"-s\",\n   172→        help=\"List all available specs\",\n   173→    ),\n   174→    project_root: str = typer.Option(\n   175→        \".\",\n   176→        \"--project-root\",\n   177→        \"-p\",\n   178→        help=\"Root directory of the project\",\n   179→    ),\n   180→    format: str = typer.Option(\n   181→        \"text\",\n   182→        \"--format\",\n   183→        \"-f\",\n   184→        help=\"Output format (text or json)\",\n   185→    ),\n   186→):\n   187→    \"\"\"List OpenSpec resources.\n   188→\n   189→    Use --specs to list all available specs in openspec/specs/.\n   190→    \"\"\"\n   191→    root = Path(project_root).resolve()\n   192→\n   193→    if not specs:\n   194→        # Default: show help\n   195→        typer.echo(ctx.get_help())\n   196→        raise typer.Exit()\n   197→\n   198→    # List specs\n   199→    spec_list = list_specs(root)\n   200→\n   201→    if format == \"json\":\n   202→        typer.echo(json.dumps(spec_list, indent=2, default=str))\n   203→    else:\n   204→        if not spec_list:\n   205→            typer.echo(typer.style(\"No specs found in openspec/specs/\", fg=typer.colors.YELLOW))\n   206→            raise typer.Exit(0)\n   207→\n   208→        typer.echo(f\"\\n{'=' * 60}\")\n   209→        typer.echo(\"Available Specs\")\n   210→        typer.echo(f\"{'=' * 60}\\n\")\n   211→\n   212→        for spec in spec_list:\n   213→            typer.echo(typer.style(f\"  {spec['name']}\", fg=typer.colors.GREEN, bold=True))\n   214→            typer.echo(f\"  Path: {spec['path']}\")\n   215→            if spec['purpose']:\n   216→                # Truncate purpose if too long\n   217→                purpose = spec['purpose']\n   218→                if len(purpose) > 100:\n   219→                    purpose = purpose[:97] + \"...\"\n   220→                typer.echo(f\"  Purpose: {purpose}\")\n   221→            typer.echo()\n   222→\n   223→        typer.echo(f\"Total: {len(spec_list)} spec(s)\")\n   224→\n   225→    raise typer.Exit(code=0)\n   226→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e569dacb-b70b-4c90-930f-0ca840cf5264","uuid":"a9f86d64-6fa4-4cd4-b020-f8fffff7aa6d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/verify-openspec-commands/tools/se3_tools/commands/openspec.py","content":"\"\"\"OpenSpec CLI commands for SE 3.0.\n\nProvides commands for managing the openspec/ directory structure:\n- openspec init: Initialize the openspec/ directory structure\n- openspec list --specs: List all available specs\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nimport typer\n\nfrom ..utils import parse_spec\n\napp = typer.Typer(name=\"openspec\", help=\"Manage OpenSpec directory and specs\")\n\n\ndef initialize_openspec(project_root: Path, force: bool = False) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Initialize the openspec/ directory structure.\n\n    Args:\n        project_root: Root directory of the project\n        force: Reinitialize even if already exists\n\n    Returns:\n        Dict with created directories and status\n    \"\"\"\n    result = {\n        \"created\": [],\n        \"existing\": [],\n        \"success\": True,\n        \"message\": \"\",\n    }\n\n    openspec_dir = project_root / \"openspec\"\n\n    # Check if already initialized\n    if openspec_dir.exists() and not force:\n        # Check if all required subdirectories exist\n        required_dirs = [\"specs\", \"changes\", \"changes/archive\"]\n        all_exist = all((openspec_dir / d).exists() for d in required_dirs)\n\n        if all_exist:\n            result[\"message\"] = \"OpenSpec directory already initialized. Use --force to reinitialize.\"\n            result[\"existing\"] = [str(openspec_dir / d) for d in required_dirs]\n            return result\n\n    # Create directory structure\n    dirs_to_create = [\n        openspec_dir / \"specs\",\n        openspec_dir / \"changes\",\n        openspec_dir / \"changes\" / \"archive\",\n    ]\n\n    for dir_path in dirs_to_create:\n        if dir_path.exists():\n            result[\"existing\"].append(str(dir_path))\n        else:\n            dir_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            result[\"created\"].append(str(dir_path))\n\n    result[\"message\"] = f\"OpenSpec initialized: {len(result['created'])} directories created\"\n    return result\n\n\ndef list_specs(project_root: Path) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    List all available specs in openspec/specs/.\n\n    Args:\n        project_root: Root directory of the project\n\n    Returns:\n        List of spec dicts with name, path, and purpose\n    \"\"\"\n    specs = []\n    specs_dir = project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n\n    if not specs_dir.exists():\n        return specs\n\n    for spec_dir in sorted(specs_dir.iterdir()):\n        if not spec_dir.is_dir():\n            continue\n\n        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n        if not spec_file.exists():\n            continue\n\n        spec_info = {\n            \"name\": spec_dir.name,\n            \"path\": str(spec_file.relative_to(project_root)),\n            \"purpose\": None,\n        }\n\n        # Try to parse the spec file to extract purpose\n        try:\n            parsed = parse_spec(str(spec_file))\n            if parsed.get(\"purpose\"):\n                spec_info[\"purpose\"] = parsed[\"purpose\"]\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\n        specs.append(spec_info)\n\n    return specs\n\n\n@app.callback()\ndef openspec_callback(ctx: typer.Context):\n    \"\"\"Manage OpenSpec directory and specs.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\n@app.command(name=\"init\")\ndef init_cmd(\n    force: bool = typer.Option(\n        False,\n        \"--force\",\n        \"-f\",\n        help=\"Reinitialize even if already initialized\",\n    ),\n    project_root: str = typer.Option(\n        \".\",\n        \"--project-root\",\n        \"-p\",\n        help=\"Root directory of the project\",\n    ),\n    format: str = typer.Option(\n        \"text\",\n        \"--format\",\n        \"-f\",\n        help=\"Output format (text or json)\",\n    ),\n):\n    \"\"\"Initialize the openspec/ directory structure.\n\n    Creates the following directories:\n    - openspec/specs/        # Source of truth for requirements\n    - openspec/changes/      # Active changes\n    - openspec/changes/archive/  # Archived changes\n    \"\"\"\n    root = Path(project_root).resolve()\n    result = initialize_openspec(root, force)\n\n    if format == \"json\":\n        typer.echo(json.dumps(result, indent=2, default=str))\n    else:\n        if result[\"created\"]:\n            typer.echo(typer.style(\"Created directories:\", fg=typer.colors.GREEN))\n            for d in result[\"created\"]:\n                typer.echo(f\"  - {d}\")\n\n        if result[\"existing\"]:\n            typer.echo(typer.style(\"Existing directories:\", fg=typer.colors.YELLOW))\n            for d in result[\"existing\"]:\n                typer.echo(f\"  - {d}\")\n\n        typer.echo(f\"\\n{result['message']}\")\n\n    raise typer.Exit(code=0 if result[\"success\"] else 1)\n\n\n@app.command(name=\"list\")\ndef list_cmd(\n    specs: bool = typer.Option(\n        False,\n        \"--specs\",\n        \"-s\",\n        help=\"List all available specs\",\n    ),\n    project_root: str = typer.Option(\n        \".\",\n        \"--project-root\",\n        \"-p\",\n        help=\"Root directory of the project\",\n    ),\n    format: str = typer.Option(\n        \"text\",\n        \"--format\",\n        \"-f\",\n        help=\"Output format (text or json)\",\n    ),\n):\n    \"\"\"List OpenSpec resources.\n\n    Use --specs to list all available specs in openspec/specs/.\n    \"\"\"\n    root = Path(project_root).resolve()\n\n    if not specs:\n        # Default: show help\n        typer.echo(ctx.get_help())\n        raise typer.Exit()\n\n    # List specs\n    spec_list = list_specs(root)\n\n    if format == \"json\":\n        typer.echo(json.dumps(spec_list, indent=2, default=str))\n    else:\n        if not spec_list:\n            typer.echo(typer.style(\"No specs found in openspec/specs/\", fg=typer.colors.YELLOW))\n            raise typer.Exit(0)\n\n        typer.echo(f\"\\n{'=' * 60}\")\n        typer.echo(\"Available Specs\")\n        typer.echo(f\"{'=' * 60}\\n\")\n\n        for spec in spec_list:\n            typer.echo(typer.style(f\"  {spec['name']}\", fg=typer.colors.GREEN, bold=True))\n            typer.echo(f\"  Path: {spec['path']}\")\n            if spec['purpose']:\n                # Truncate purpose if too long\n                purpose = spec['purpose']\n                if len(purpose) > 100:\n                    purpose = purpose[:97] + \"...\"\n                typer.echo(f\"  Purpose: {purpose}\")\n            typer.echo()\n\n        typer.echo(f\"Total: {len(spec_list)} spec(s)\")\n\n    raise typer.Exit(code=0)\n","numLines":226,"startLine":1,"totalLines":226}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_17tx5v5YplWsSNst8VWWpphM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"Tests for the openspec CLI commands.\n     2→\n     3→Tests cover:\n     4→- openspec init: Initialize the openspec/ directory structure\n     5→- openspec list --specs: List all available specs\n     6→\"\"\"\n     7→\n     8→import json\n     9→import os\n    10→import sys\n    11→import tempfile\n    12→from pathlib import Path\n    13→from unittest.mock import patch, MagicMock\n    14→\n    15→import pytest\n    16→\n    17→# Add tools to path for imports\n    18→sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"tools\"))\n    19→\n    20→from se3_tools.commands.openspec import initialize_openspec, list_specs\n    21→\n    22→\n    23→# =============================================================================\n    24→# OpenSpec Init Tests\n    25→# =============================================================================\n    26→\n    27→class TestOpenSpecInit:\n    28→    \"\"\"Test openspec init command.\"\"\"\n    29→\n    30→    def setup_method(self):\n    31→        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n    32→        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\n    33→\n    34→    def test_initialize_openspec_creates_directories(self):\n    35→        \"\"\"openspec init should create openspec/, specs/, changes/, changes/archive/.\"\"\"\n    36→        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n    37→\n    38→        assert result[\"success\"] is True\n    39→        assert len(result[\"created\"]) == 3\n    40→        assert len(result[\"existing\"]) == 0\n    41→\n    42→        # Verify directories exist\n    43→        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\").exists()\n    44→        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"changes\").exists()\n    45→        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"changes\" / \"archive\").exists()\n    46→\n    47→    def test_initialize_openspec_idempotent(self):\n    48→        \"\"\"openspec init should be idempotent - not fail if run twice.\"\"\"\n    49→        # First init\n    50→        result1 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n    51→        assert result1[\"success\"] is True\n    52→        assert len(result1[\"created\"]) == 3\n    53→\n    54→        # Second init without force\n    55→        result2 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n    56→        assert result2[\"success\"] is True\n    57→        assert len(result2[\"existing\"]) == 3\n    58→        assert \"already initialized\" in result2[\"message\"].lower()\n    59→\n    60→    def test_initialize_openspec_with_force(self):\n    61→        \"\"\"openspec init --force should reinitialize even if exists.\"\"\"\n    62→        # First init\n    63→        initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n    64→\n    65→        # Force reinit\n    66→        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root, force=True)\n    67→        assert result[\"success\"] is True\n    68→        # With force, it still reports existing since directories already exist\n    69→        assert len(result[\"existing\"]) == 3\n    70→\n    71→\n    72→# =============================================================================\n    73→# OpenSpec List Tests\n    74→# =============================================================================\n    75→\n    76→class TestOpenSpecList:\n    77→    \"\"\"Test openspec list --specs command.\"\"\"\n    78→\n    79→    def setup_method(self):\n    80→        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n    81→        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\n    82→\n    83→        # Create openspec structure\n    84→        self.specs_dir = self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n    85→        self.specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n    86→\n    87→    def _create_spec(self, name: str, purpose: str = None):\n    88→        \"\"\"Helper to create a spec file.\"\"\"\n    89→        spec_dir = self.specs_dir / name\n    90→        spec_dir.mkdir()\n    91→\n    92→        content = f\"# {name} Specification\\n\\n\"\n    93→        content += \"## Purpose\\n\\n\"\n    94→        if purpose:\n    95→            content += f\"{purpose}\\n\"\n    96→        content += \"\\n## Requirements\\n\\n\"\n    97→        content += \"### Requirement: Test\\n\\n\"\n    98→        content += \"The system SHALL test.\\n\"\n    99→\n   100→        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n   101→        spec_file.write_text(content)\n   102→        return spec_file\n   103→\n   104→    def test_list_specs_empty(self):\n   105→        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should return empty list when no specs.\"\"\"\n   106→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n   107→        assert specs == []\n   108→\n   109→    def test_list_specs_single(self):\n   110→        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should list a single spec.\"\"\"\n   111→        self._create_spec(\"test-spec\", \"Test purpose description\")\n   112→\n   113→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n   114→        assert len(specs) == 1\n   115→        assert specs[0][\"name\"] == \"test-spec\"\n   116→        assert \"openspec/specs/test-spec/spec.md\" in specs[0][\"path\"]\n   117→        assert \"Test purpose\" in specs[0][\"purpose\"]\n   118→\n   119→    def test_list_specs_multiple(self):\n   120→        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should list multiple specs sorted by name.\"\"\"\n   121→        self._create_spec(\"zebra-spec\", \"Zebra spec purpose\")\n   122→        self._create_spec(\"alpha-spec\", \"Alpha spec purpose\")\n   123→        self._create_spec(\"beta-spec\", \"Beta spec purpose\")\n   124→\n   125→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n   126→        assert len(specs) == 3\n   127→\n   128→        # Should be sorted alphabetically\n   129→        assert specs[0][\"name\"] == \"alpha-spec\"\n   130→        assert specs[1][\"name\"] == \"beta-spec\"\n   131→        assert specs[2][\"name\"] == \"zebra-spec\"\n   132→\n   133→    def test_list_specs_ignores_non_spec_dirs(self):\n   134→        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should ignore directories without spec.md.\"\"\"\n   135→        # Create a spec\n   136→        self._create_spec(\"valid-spec\", \"Valid spec\")\n   137→\n   138→        # Create a directory without spec.md\n   139→        (self.specs_dir / \"empty-dir\").mkdir()\n   140→\n   141→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n   142→        assert len(specs) == 1\n   143→        assert specs[0][\"name\"] == \"valid-spec\"\n   144→\n   145→    def test_list_specs_no_openspec_dir(self):\n   146→        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should handle missing openspec directory.\"\"\"\n   147→        # Remove openspec directory\n   148→        import shutil\n   149→        shutil.rmtree(self.project_root / \"openspec\")\n   150→\n   151→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n   152→        assert specs == []\n   153→\n   154→\n   155→# =============================================================================\n   156→# CLI Integration Tests\n   157→# =============================================================================\n   158→\n   159→class TestOpenSpecCLI:\n   160→    \"\"\"Test openspec CLI commands via typer.\"\"\"\n   161→\n   162→    def setup_method(self):\n   163→        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n   164→        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\n   165→\n   166→    def test_cli_init_command(self):\n   167→        \"\"\"Test the CLI init command directly.\"\"\"\n   168→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n   169→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n   170→\n   171→        runner = CliRunner()\n   172→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"init\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root)])\n   173→\n   174→        assert result.exit_code == 0\n   175→        assert \"Created directories\" in result.output\n   176→\n   177→        # Verify directories exist\n   178→        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\").exists()\n   179→\n   180→    def test_cli_list_specs_command(self):\n   181→        \"\"\"Test the CLI list --specs command.\"\"\"\n   182→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n   183→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n   184→\n   185→        # Create a spec\n   186→        specs_dir = self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n   187→        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n   188→        spec_dir = specs_dir / \"test-spec\"\n   189→        spec_dir.mkdir()\n   190→        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n   191→        spec_file.write_text(\"# Test Spec\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nTest purpose.\\n\")\n   192→\n   193→        runner = CliRunner()\n   194→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"list\", \"--specs\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root)])\n   195→\n   196→        assert result.exit_code == 0\n   197→        assert \"test-spec\" in result.output\n   198→        assert \"Test purpose\" in result.output\n   199→\n   200→    def test_cli_list_specs_json_format(self):\n   201→        \"\"\"Test the CLI list --specs --format json command.\"\"\"\n   202→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n   203→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n   204→\n   205→        # Create a spec\n   206→        specs_dir = self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n   207→        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n   208→        spec_dir = specs_dir / \"test-spec\"\n   209→        spec_dir.mkdir()\n   210→        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n   211→        spec_file.write_text(\"# Test Spec\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nTest purpose.\\n\")\n   212→\n   213→        runner = CliRunner()\n   214→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"list\", \"--specs\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root), \"--format\", \"json\"])\n   215→\n   216→        assert result.exit_code == 0\n   217→        data = json.loads(result.output)\n   218→        assert len(data) == 1\n   219→        assert data[0][\"name\"] == \"test-spec\"\n   220→\n   221→    def test_cli_init_json_format(self):\n   222→        \"\"\"Test the CLI init --format json command.\"\"\"\n   223→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n   224→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n   225→\n   226→        runner = CliRunner()\n   227→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"init\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root), \"--format\", \"json\"])\n   228→\n   229→        assert result.exit_code == 0\n   230→        data = json.loads(result.output)\n   231→        assert data[\"success\"] is True\n   232→        assert len(data[\"created\"]) == 3\n   233→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e569dacb-b70b-4c90-930f-0ca840cf5264","uuid":"61bffdb3-438d-4431-a4f2-f60adf339d45","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/verify-openspec-commands/tests/test_openspec.py","content":"\"\"\"Tests for the openspec CLI commands.\n\nTests cover:\n- openspec init: Initialize the openspec/ directory structure\n- openspec list --specs: List all available specs\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unittest.mock import patch, MagicMock\n\nimport pytest\n\n# Add tools to path for imports\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"tools\"))\n\nfrom se3_tools.commands.openspec import initialize_openspec, list_specs\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# OpenSpec Init Tests\n# =============================================================================\n\nclass TestOpenSpecInit:\n    \"\"\"Test openspec init command.\"\"\"\n\n    def setup_method(self):\n        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\n\n    def test_initialize_openspec_creates_directories(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec init should create openspec/, specs/, changes/, changes/archive/.\"\"\"\n        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n\n        assert result[\"success\"] is True\n        assert len(result[\"created\"]) == 3\n        assert len(result[\"existing\"]) == 0\n\n        # Verify directories exist\n        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\").exists()\n        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"changes\").exists()\n        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"changes\" / \"archive\").exists()\n\n    def test_initialize_openspec_idempotent(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec init should be idempotent - not fail if run twice.\"\"\"\n        # First init\n        result1 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n        assert result1[\"success\"] is True\n        assert len(result1[\"created\"]) == 3\n\n        # Second init without force\n        result2 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n        assert result2[\"success\"] is True\n        assert len(result2[\"existing\"]) == 3\n        assert \"already initialized\" in result2[\"message\"].lower()\n\n    def test_initialize_openspec_with_force(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec init --force should reinitialize even if exists.\"\"\"\n        # First init\n        initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\n\n        # Force reinit\n        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root, force=True)\n        assert result[\"success\"] is True\n        # With force, it still reports existing since directories already exist\n        assert len(result[\"existing\"]) == 3\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# OpenSpec List Tests\n# =============================================================================\n\nclass TestOpenSpecList:\n    \"\"\"Test openspec list --specs command.\"\"\"\n\n    def setup_method(self):\n        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\n\n        # Create openspec structure\n        self.specs_dir = self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n        self.specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n\n    def _create_spec(self, name: str, purpose: str = None):\n        \"\"\"Helper to create a spec file.\"\"\"\n        spec_dir = self.specs_dir / name\n        spec_dir.mkdir()\n\n        content = f\"# {name} Specification\\n\\n\"\n        content += \"## Purpose\\n\\n\"\n        if purpose:\n            content += f\"{purpose}\\n\"\n        content += \"\\n## Requirements\\n\\n\"\n        content += \"### Requirement: Test\\n\\n\"\n        content += \"The system SHALL test.\\n\"\n\n        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n        spec_file.write_text(content)\n        return spec_file\n\n    def test_list_specs_empty(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should return empty list when no specs.\"\"\"\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n        assert specs == []\n\n    def test_list_specs_single(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should list a single spec.\"\"\"\n        self._create_spec(\"test-spec\", \"Test purpose description\")\n\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n        assert len(specs) == 1\n        assert specs[0][\"name\"] == \"test-spec\"\n        assert \"openspec/specs/test-spec/spec.md\" in specs[0][\"path\"]\n        assert \"Test purpose\" in specs[0][\"purpose\"]\n\n    def test_list_specs_multiple(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should list multiple specs sorted by name.\"\"\"\n        self._create_spec(\"zebra-spec\", \"Zebra spec purpose\")\n        self._create_spec(\"alpha-spec\", \"Alpha spec purpose\")\n        self._create_spec(\"beta-spec\", \"Beta spec purpose\")\n\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n        assert len(specs) == 3\n\n        # Should be sorted alphabetically\n        assert specs[0][\"name\"] == \"alpha-spec\"\n        assert specs[1][\"name\"] == \"beta-spec\"\n        assert specs[2][\"name\"] == \"zebra-spec\"\n\n    def test_list_specs_ignores_non_spec_dirs(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should ignore directories without spec.md.\"\"\"\n        # Create a spec\n        self._create_spec(\"valid-spec\", \"Valid spec\")\n\n        # Create a directory without spec.md\n        (self.specs_dir / \"empty-dir\").mkdir()\n\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n        assert len(specs) == 1\n        assert specs[0][\"name\"] == \"valid-spec\"\n\n    def test_list_specs_no_openspec_dir(self):\n        \"\"\"openspec list --specs should handle missing openspec directory.\"\"\"\n        # Remove openspec directory\n        import shutil\n        shutil.rmtree(self.project_root / \"openspec\")\n\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\n        assert specs == []\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# CLI Integration Tests\n# =============================================================================\n\nclass TestOpenSpecCLI:\n    \"\"\"Test openspec CLI commands via typer.\"\"\"\n\n    def setup_method(self):\n        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\n\n    def test_cli_init_command(self):\n        \"\"\"Test the CLI init command directly.\"\"\"\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n\n        runner = CliRunner()\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"init\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root)])\n\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\n        assert \"Created directories\" in result.output\n\n        # Verify directories exist\n        assert (self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\").exists()\n\n    def test_cli_list_specs_command(self):\n        \"\"\"Test the CLI list --specs command.\"\"\"\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n\n        # Create a spec\n        specs_dir = self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n        spec_dir = specs_dir / \"test-spec\"\n        spec_dir.mkdir()\n        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n        spec_file.write_text(\"# Test Spec\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nTest purpose.\\n\")\n\n        runner = CliRunner()\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"list\", \"--specs\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root)])\n\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\n        assert \"test-spec\" in result.output\n        assert \"Test purpose\" in result.output\n\n    def test_cli_list_specs_json_format(self):\n        \"\"\"Test the CLI list --specs --format json command.\"\"\"\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n\n        # Create a spec\n        specs_dir = self.project_root / \"openspec\" / \"specs\"\n        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n        spec_dir = specs_dir / \"test-spec\"\n        spec_dir.mkdir()\n        spec_file = spec_dir / \"spec.md\"\n        spec_file.write_text(\"# Test Spec\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nTest purpose.\\n\")\n\n        runner = CliRunner()\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"list\", \"--specs\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root), \"--format\", \"json\"])\n\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\n        data = json.loads(result.output)\n        assert len(data) == 1\n        assert data[0][\"name\"] == \"test-spec\"\n\n    def test_cli_init_json_format(self):\n        \"\"\"Test the CLI init --format json command.\"\"\"\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\n\n        runner = CliRunner()\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\"init\", \"--project-root\", str(self.project_root), \"--format\", \"json\"])\n\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\n        data = json.loads(result.output)\n        assert data[\"success\"] is True\n        assert len(data[\"created\"]) == 3\n","numLines":233,"startLine":1,"totalLines":233}}}
